# =============================================================================
# Poly VST3 Plugin - .gitignore
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored agent skills. Skills are installed, not authored here: the five
# jk-standards ones come from `jk-standards install-skills --dest .claude/skills`
# and are pinned by skills-lock.json, and other agent harnesses install their own
# defaults alongside them. The rule is deny-by-default rather than an explicit
# list of the five, because an explicit list leaves any *newly* installed skill
# untracked-but-unignored, where the next `git add -A` sweeps it into a commit —
# which is exactly how 294 files of unrelated vendored skills once landed here.
# poly-site is the one poly-local, hand-authored skill, so it is re-included.
#
# `.claude/skills/*` (not `.claude/skills/`) is required: git will not descend
# into an excluded directory, so the negation below could not re-include
# poly-site if the parent were excluded wholesale.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/poly-site/

# Generic-agent skills dir (`install-skills` default --dest). Nothing in poly
# reads it; it exists only when a harness installs skills without --dest.
.agents/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build Directories
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
Build/
out/
cmake-build-*/
**/build/
**/Build/
**/out/
build-test/
build-*/

# Cubase-phase run output (probe JSONL, phase status, window topology, Cubase
# prefs/logs). The workflow points POLY_ARTIFACT_DIR at the run's staging dir,
# but scripts/cubase/_common.ps1 falls back to a repo-local _artifacts/ for
# by-hand dry-runs — which must never be committed.
_artifacts/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# External SDKs (downloaded during CI)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
vst3sdk/

